2.6. Lipid Metabolism
We focused on lipid metabolism and specific fatty acid (C12:0, C14:0, C16:0, C16:1, C18:0, C18:1, C18:2) synthesis while developing a metabolic model of the BSF larvae. These fatty acids were of special interest in the modeling of H. illucens larvae metabolism due to their high content in the organism, as captured by fatty acid profiling measurements. They are also of interest because of their biotechnological significance and the prospects for the optimizing, analyzing, and predicting of their yields when using bioconversion for recycling and the reduction in industrial and agricultural waste [43]. The lipid metabolism reaction complexes included in our metabolic model cover several pathways:
1.Fatty acid biosynthesis initiation (type I), PWY-5966; 2.Palmitate biosynthesis I (type I fatty acid synthase), PWY-5994;


